/-!
# The cohomology sheaves of the décalage of an invertible ideal

In Situation 0GT4 — a ringed space `(X, O_X)` together with a sheaf of ideals
`ι : I ⟶ O_X` which is locally generated by a nonzerodivisor — let `F` be a cochain complex of
`I`-torsion-free `O_X`-modules.  This file constructs the canonical isomorphism
`I^{⊗ n} ⊗ (H^n(F)/H^n(F)[I]) ⟶ H^n(η_I F)` of Tag 0F8N, where `η_I` is the Berthelot–Ogus
operator of `EtaSheaf.lean` and `H^n(F)[I]` is the subsheaf of `H^n(F)` annihilated by `I`.

## Main definitions

* `Situation`: the data of Situation 0GT4 — a sheaf of ideals locally generated by a
  nonzerodivisor on a ringed space.
* `etaCyclesIso`: the comparison `I^{⊗ n} ⊗ Z^n(F) ≅ Z^n(η_I F)` of cocycle sheaves.
* `etaHomologyMap`: the map `I^{⊗ n} ⊗ H^n(F) ⟶ H^n(η_I F)` induced by it.
* `etaCohomologyIso`: the canonical isomorphism of Tag 0F8N.

## Main results

* `etaCohomologyIso` (Tag 0F8N) is the canonical isomorphism
  `I^{⊗ n} ⊗ (H^n(F)/H^n(F)[I]) ≅ H^n(η_I F)` of cohomology sheaves.
* `etaCohomologyIso_hom` pins it down: precomposed with the twisted quotient map
  `I^{⊗ n} ⊗ H^n(F) ⟶ I^{⊗ n} ⊗ (H^n(F)/H^n(F)[I])` it is `etaHomologyMap`, and
  `etaHomologyMap_cycles` computes the latter on cocycles as `g ⊗ s ↦ g s`.
* `etaCyclesIso_hom_fst`, `etaCyclesIso_hom_snd`: the comparison of cocycle sheaves is, on the
  two projections of the fibre product defining the décalage term, the twisted inclusion of
  cocycles and zero.
* `etaHomologyMap_comp_eq_zero_iff`: a map into `I^{⊗ (n+1)} ⊗ H^{n+1}(F)` is killed by
  `etaHomologyMap` exactly when it is killed by the inclusion of the next ideal power, which is
  what identifies the kernel with the `I`-torsion.
* `idealPowerAnnihilatorIsKernel`: the twisted torsion subsheaf `I^{⊗ (n+1)} ⊗ M[I]` is the
  kernel of `I^{⊗ (n+1)} ⊗ M ⟶ I^{⊗ n} ⊗ M`.

## Implementation notes

The map made canonical is the one the source writes down: a local section `g` of `I^{⊗ n}` and
a local cocycle `s` of `F^n` are sent to the local section `g s` of `(η_I F)^n ⊆ I^{⊗ n} ⊗ F^n`.
Categorically this is the lift `I^{⊗ n} ⊗ Z^n(F) ⟶ (η_I F)^n` of the twisted inclusion of
cocycles along the first projection of the defining fibre product, with second component zero
(`etaCyclesTerm`); `etaCyclesIso_hom_fst` and `etaCyclesIso_hom_snd` say exactly that, and the
lift is uniquely determined by them because its target is a fibre product.  No choice is made
anywhere: `etaCohomologyIso` is the comparison of two cokernels of the *same* map, produced by
`IsColimit.coconePointUniqueUpToIso`, and `etaCohomologyIso_hom` records the only property such
a comparison can have.  In particular the isomorphism is not obtained from an existence
statement.

The argument is the one of the source, but run in the abelian category of sheaves of modules
rather than on stalks.  The source reduces to the affine statement Tag 0F7P through the stalk
comparison Tag 0GT6; that route would need the stalk of `I^{⊗ n} ⊗ -`, of the torsion subsheaf
and of homology, all of which are private to `EtaSheaf.lean`.  What replaces it is the
observation that each of the three steps of Tag 0F7P is a statement about kernels and cokernels
that `I^{⊗ n} ⊗ -` — an autoequivalence, hence exact — transports:

* `Z^n(η_I F) ≅ I^{⊗ n} ⊗ Z^n(F)` (`etaCyclesIso`), because a cocycle of `η_I F` is a section
  of `I^{⊗ n} ⊗ F^n` killed by the differential, the condition defining `(η_I F)^n` being
  automatic for such a section;
* the induced `I^{⊗ n} ⊗ H^n(F) ⟶ H^n(η_I F)` is epi (`etaHomologyMap_epi`), since it factors
  the epi `I^{⊗ n} ⊗ Z^n(F) ≅ Z^n(η_I F) ↠ H^n(η_I F)`;
* its kernel is the twisted torsion (`etaHomologyMap_comp_eq_zero_iff`): a coboundary of
  `η_I F` in degree `n + 1` is, under the comparison, a section of `I^{⊗ n} ⊗ Z^{n+1}(F)`
  rather than of `I^{⊗ (n+1)} ⊗ Z^{n+1}(F)`, which is the categorical form of "`f` times a
  cocycle is a coboundary".  Both directions are checked up to refinements, the abelian
  category not being a category of modules.

The hypotheses used are `Mono ι` together with invertibility of `I`, that is condition (2) of
Tag 0GT3 rather than condition (1) demanded by Situation 0GT4.  This is formally weaker, hence
the statements are formally stronger, and it is the generalization sanctioned by the footnote
to Situation 0GT4; `EtaSheaf.lean` and `EtaSheafTensor.lean` are set up the same way, and
`Situation` below records condition (1) verbatim for reference.  The implication from condition
(1) to invertibility is Tag 0GT3, which this repository does not formalize, so no bridge from
`Situation` to the hypotheses of the main theorem is available here.

Multiplication by the ideal, `idealMultiplication`, and the identification of the torsion
subsheaf `M[I]` with the kernel of `I^{⊗ (n+1)} ⊗ M ⟶ I^{⊗ n} ⊗ M` are developed here from
scratch: `EtaSheafTensor.lean` has the multiplication map, but privately, and nothing in the
library relates the annihilator subsheaf of `IdealTorsionFree.lean` to that kernel.

Two spellings of the structure sheaf of rings meet here, exactly as in `EtaSheaf.lean`:
`structureSheaf X.sheaf`, over which the tensor-power calculus is stated, and
`structureSheafRing X`, which indexes the annihilator subsheaf of
`IdealTorsionFree.lean`.  They are the same sheaf of rings but do not unfold below `default`
transparency, so the proofs below follow the discipline of `EtaSheaf.lean`: the goal is put in
a single spelling with `change`, and steps that `rw` cannot match are supplied as chains of
ground equations through `congrArg`, `Eq.trans` and `calc`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F8N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F8N)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GT4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GT4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GT3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GT3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GT5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GT5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GT6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GT6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F7P](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F7P)
-/

